    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3025" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăpĭna</span></b> , ae,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				poor and small town in Apulia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 11,
				16, § 144</span></i>.—Hence, in the
			plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăpĭnae</span></b> , prov. (as tricae, q. v.),
				<i>trifles</i>, <i>worthless
			things</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apinae tricaeque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					14, 1, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 113, 2</span></i>
			(some regard this form as from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφανής</span>, obscure, of no account).</div>
